<DemoExample Title="URL Matching" RazorCode="@example11RazorCode" Id="example11" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        In the <b>Automatic</b> mode the option whose URL matches the current page is selected. <b>Match</b> sets the rule
        for the whole nav, and the <b>Match</b> of an option overrides it: <b>Exact</b>, <b>Prefix</b>, <b>Wildcard</b>
        (<b>?</b> is one character but <b>/</b>, <b>*</b> any run of them, <b>**</b> anything) or <b>Regex</b>. The query
        string is ignored, and <b>Exact</b> and <b>Prefix</b> also ignore the letter case and a trailing slash.
        <b>AdditionalUrls</b> gives an option more URLs to light up on. The navs below match the URL of this page.
    </div>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Exact (the default)</div><br />
    <BitNav TItem="BitNavOption" FitWidth>
        <BitNavOption Text="Nav (this page)" IconName="@BitIconName.GlobalNavButton" Url="/components/nav" />
        <BitNavOption Text="Pivot" IconName="@BitIconName.MiniExpand" Url="/components/pivot" />
    </BitNav>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Prefix</div><br />
    <BitNav TItem="BitNavOption" Match="BitNavMatch.Prefix" FitWidth>
        <BitNavOption Text="Components (/components)" IconName="@BitIconName.F12DevTools" Url="/components" />
        <BitNavOption Text="Iconography (/iconography)" IconName="@BitIconName.AppIconDefault" Url="/iconography" />
    </BitNav>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Wildcard</div><br />
    @* The URL of a Wildcard or Regex option is a pattern rather than a route, so these options are
       disabled: they still light up on a match, but a click cannot navigate to a URL no page answers. *@
    <BitNav TItem="BitNavOption" Match="BitNavMatch.Wildcard" FitWidth>
        <BitNavOption Text="A component page (/components/*)" IconName="@BitIconName.F12DevTools" Url="/components/*" IsEnabled="false" />
        <BitNavOption Text="A pro page (/pro/**)" IconName="@BitIconName.Trophy2" Url="/pro/**" IsEnabled="false" />
    </BitNav>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Regex</div><br />
    <BitNav TItem="BitNavOption" Match="BitNavMatch.Regex" FitWidth>
        <BitNavOption Text="Nav or NavBar (^/components/nav(bar)?$)" IconName="@BitIconName.GlobalNavButton" Url="^/components/nav(bar)?$" IsEnabled="false" />
        <BitNavOption Text="A page starting with P (^/components/p)" IconName="@BitIconName.Page" Url="^/components/p" IsEnabled="false" />
    </BitNav>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Match of an option &amp; AdditionalUrls</div><br />
    <BitNav TItem="BitNavOption" Match="BitNavMatch.Exact" FitWidth>
        <BitNavOption Text="Components (its own Prefix)" IconName="@BitIconName.F12DevTools" Url="/components" Match="BitNavMatch.Prefix" />
        <BitNavOption Text="Pivot (the Exact of the nav)" IconName="@BitIconName.MiniExpand" Url="/components/pivot" />
    </BitNav>
    <br /><br />
    <BitNav TItem="BitNavOption" FitWidth>
        <BitNavOption Text="Navigation (also /components/nav)"
                      IconName="@BitIconName.GlobalNavButton"
                      Url="/components/navbar"
                      AdditionalUrls="@(["/components/nav", "/components/breadcrumb"])" />
        <BitNavOption Text="Inputs" IconName="@BitIconName.TextField" Url="/components/textfield" />
    </BitNav>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Accessibility" RazorCode="@example12RazorCode" Id="example12">
    <div>
        The nav is a <b>nav</b> landmark: name it with <b>AriaLabel</b> when a page has more than one. The selected option
        carries <b>aria-current</b> (its <b>AriaCurrent</b> picks the value), a <b>Description</b> is announced as the
        option's description, and a parent reports <b>aria-expanded</b>. A parent without a URL toggles on a click anywhere
        on it; a parent with one navigates, so its chevron becomes a button of its own, named by
        <b>ExpandAriaLabel</b> / <b>CollapseAriaLabel</b>.
        <br /><br />
        Keyboard: <b>Tab</b> moves between the options, <b>↑</b> <b>↓</b> <b>Home</b> <b>End</b> walk the visible ones,
        <b>→</b> opens a branch and then steps into it, <b>←</b> closes it and then steps out, <b>*</b> opens every
        sibling, and typing jumps to the next option starting with it. Collapse <b>Navs</b>: the branch that holds the
        current page takes the look of the selection, so the reader never loses it.
    </div>
    <br />
    <BitNav TItem="BitNavOption" AriaLabel="Components" FitWidth>
        <BitNavOption Text="Navs"
                      IconName="@BitIconName.GlobalNavButton"
                      Url="/components"
                      Description="Links to the areas of an app"
                      ExpandAriaLabel="Show the navs"
                      CollapseAriaLabel="Hide the navs">
            <BitNavOption Text="Nav" Url="/components/nav" />
            <BitNavOption Text="NavBar" Url="/components/navbar" />
            <BitNavOption Text="Breadcrumb" Url="/components/breadcrumb" />
        </BitNavOption>
        <BitNavOption Text="Inputs" IconName="@BitIconName.TextField" Description="Fields that take a value">
            <BitNavOption Text="TextField" Url="/components/textfield" />
            <BitNavOption Text="Dropdown" Url="/components/dropdown" />
        </BitNavOption>
